## How Investec Programmable Banking is used

| API | Purpose |
|-----|---------|
| OAuth2 authorisation endpoint | Read-only consent flow for the holder |
| `GET /za/pb/v1/accounts` | Discover the holder's accounts |
| `GET /za/pb/v1/accounts/{id}/balance` | Evaluate current-balance claim |
| `GET /za/pb/v1/accounts/{id}/transactions` | Evaluate inflow, tenure, salary, overdraft claims |

**Privacy rule**: the Investec API is called once per credential-issuance request. After
`PredicateService` reduces raw transactions to boolean thresholds, the `List<Transaction>`
goes out of scope and is garbage-collected. No transaction data reaches the database, the
logs, or the response body — ever.

The adapter pattern (`InvestecClient` interface) means a `FixtureInvestecClient` (default dev
profile) returns deterministic SA fixture data, so the entire flow is demonstrable without real
Investec credentials.

