## Credential format

SD-JWT VC (IETF draft-ietf-oauth-selective-disclosure-jwt) signed with the issuer's EC P-256 key.

- Issuer identity: `did:web` — JWKS served at `/.well-known/jwks.json`.
- Each claim is a separate disclosure: `BASE64URL(["<salt>","<claim_name>",<claim_value>])`.
- JWT payload contains `_sd` (array of SHA-256 hashes of all disclosures) and never the raw values.
- Presentation = issuer JWT + only the chosen disclosures + trailing `~`.

---

## Privacy-by-design properties

| Property | Enforcement |
|----------|-------------|
| No raw transactions at rest | `PredicateService` processes in memory; no transaction entity exists |
| Threshold-only credentials | Claims certify "≥ R30,000", never exact figures |
| Selective disclosure | Unrevealed disclosures are stripped; verifier cannot infer their count |
| Read-only bank access | Investec OAuth2 scope is `accounts` only |

